MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like a natural next choice after Old Sock because the Clapton connection and relaxed blues sound matched what I wanted to hear today.",
    "Made Up Mind appealed to me because soulful vocals and blues guitar connect with my interest in Memphis and Hendrix; those musical qualities matter more to me than a broad roots-music resemblance."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Invisible Empire // Crescent Moon felt too quiet and acoustic for my current interest in blues guitar and roots-rock energy.",
    "Let's Be Still leaned toward folk harmonies when I wanted blues and soul. Same Trailer Different Park made sense after Blown Away, but country was less compelling to me today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A broad connection to roots music seemed to count too much, even though acoustic folk and guitar-led blues satisfy different listening moods for me.",
    "My country listening seemed to carry more weight than it deserved for this visit, when I was leaning toward the blues side of my recent choices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of an artist connection, blues guitar, and the right mood made The Breeze especially appealing after Old Sock.",
    "Being relevant does not mean I will choose an album immediately: I only wanted two picks today, and some other appealing records would need a sample or another visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues and roots music, but sometimes stretched that interest beyond the guitar, soul, and mood I wanted today."
}
